A||||2||JetroGT||Learning from experience||||14||
Z||000000||JetroGT||08-13-2001||06:25 PM||||Today I had to change my Oil Sending Unit. I've never done it but it looked easy enough. I just wanted to show how easy it was for people that have never changed one.<BR>First I took the battery out.<BR>Then I put a cressen wrench on the base.<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Base.jpg">  <BR>Then I took a 9/16 wrench and turned it off.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/9_16ths.jpg"> <BR>Put a new one on and I'm done. <BR>I tried to put a pipe wrench on the bigger plastic top and it only resulted in the seperation of the plastic to metal base of the sensor. <BR>This was an easy one so don't pay someone else 50 bucks an hour...unless it's me.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>Thanks for the space!<p>[This message has been edited by JetroGT (edited 08-13-2001).]||||reg||14
Z||000001||terryk||08-13-2001||10:44 PM||||You know, this is the type of quality write-up that needs to go into a *real* tech section.<P>Great presentation dude!<P>TK||||reg||14
